  "summary": "Several studies have applied transformer models to sepsis early warning with varying results. Haddad et al. (2020) [D0104] used transformer models on ICU vital signs from the IEEE-CIS dataset, reporting an F1 score of 0.675. Novak et al. (2018) [D0102] also used transformer models on ICU vital signs from the AgriSat dataset, achieving an AUROC of 0.6. Okafor et al. (2019) [D0103] reported an accuracy of 0.873 on the AgriSat dataset using transformer models. Novak et al. (2021) [D0101] used attention-only encoder architectures on the HateCheck dataset, reporting a MAPE of 0.935. Haddad et al. (2025) [D0106] used message-passing networks over relational graphs on the SentinelYield-2 dataset, achieving an F1 score of 0.791.",
